# Score Chart

A **client island** is a UI unit that ships to the browser and **hydrates**. This
one is a Svelte component drawing a bar per lead. Its contract is narrow and
one-directional: *give me leads, I give you bars.* It never scores or enriches —
those are server jobs it has no grant to do.

The body is real Svelte — markup, `<script>`, scoped `<style>` — set off by blank
lines. The `client svelte :chart do` line names the unit, placement, and language;
the rest is ordinary component source.

client svelte :chart do
  <script>
    export let leads = [];
    export let emit = () => {};
    $: ranked = [...leads].sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);
    $: top = ranked.reduce((m, l) => Math.max(m, l.score), 0) || 1;
  </script>

  <figure class="chart">
    {#each ranked as lead (lead.domain)}
      <button class="bar" class:enriched={lead.status === "enriched"}
              style="--h: {(lead.score / top) * 100}%"
              on:click={() => emit("select", lead)}>
        <span>{lead.score}</span>
        <span class="fill" />
        <span>{lead.name}</span>
      </button>
    {/each}
  </figure>

  <style>
    .chart { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: .75rem; height: 220px }
    .fill  { height: var(--h); background: var(--mint, #aee5c2); border-radius: 6px 6px 0 0 }
    .bar.enriched .fill { background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, #aee5c2 0 6px, #fbfaf3 6px 12px) }
  </style>
end

Because it's an island, it behaves identically across all three delivery modes — in
[[Live SSR]] a freshly scored lead grows its bar with no reload. The companion trend
view is the SolidJS [[Trend sparkline]].
